#: passwords.cpp:40
msgid "Echo Characters As"
msgstr "Pokazuj pismiki jako"

#: passwords.cpp:42
msgid ""
"You can select the type of visual feedback given when you enter a password "
"in kdesu. Choose one of the following options:"
"<p> "
"<ul>"
"<li><em>1 star:</em> each character you type is shown as an asterisk (*) "
"symbol.</li> "
"<li><em>3 stars:</em> three asterisks are shown for each character you "
"type.</li> "
"<li><em>no echo:</em>"
" there is no visual feedback at all, so nothing on your screen shows how "
"many characters are in your password.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""
"Móžeće tu wubrać, što ma so pokazać, hdyž zapodawaće škitne hesło "
"do kdesu. Wubjerće sej jednu ze sćěhowacych opcijow:"
"<p>"
"<ul>"
"<li><em>jedna hwěžka:</em> kóždy pismik, kotryž so zapodawa, pokazuje "
"so jako hwěžka (*).</li> "
"<li><em>tři hwěžki:</em> tři hwěžki (***) so za kóždy pismik "
"pokazuja</li> "
"<li><em>ničo:</em> žana wizuelna kontrola; ničo na wobrazowce "
"njepokazuje, kelko pismikow je we wašim škitnym hesle.</li></ul>"

#: passwords.cpp:49
msgid "&1 star"
msgstr "&1 hwěžka"

#: passwords.cpp:50
msgid "&3 stars"
msgstr "&3 hwěžki "

#: passwords.cpp:51
msgid "&No echo"
msgstr "&Ničo"

#: passwords.cpp:56
msgid "&Remember passwords"
msgstr "&Spomjatkuj sej hesło"

#: passwords.cpp:57
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, kdesu will remember your passwords for the "
"specified amount of time. Until then, you will not have to enter your "
"password again. Keep in mind that this option is insecure and may enable "
"others to damage your system."
"<p> Please <em>do not</em>"
" use this option if you are working in an insecure environment, for example, "
"on a workstation that is located in a publicly accessible area."
"<p> This option does not affect passwords explicitly set in other "
"applications, for example, your email account password in KMail."
msgstr ""
"Wubjerje-li so tuta opcija, sej kdesu waše hesła wěsty čas spomjatkuje. "
"Za tutón čas njetrjebaće swoje hesła znowa zapodać. Wopomńće pak, zo "
"tuta opcija wěstosć systema kompromituje a snano druhim zmóžni, waš "
"system znjewužiwać."
"<p>Prošu <em>njewužiwajće tutu opciju</em> w njewěstej wokolinje, na "
"př. na zjawnje přistupnym computeru."
"<p> Tuta opcija njewuskutkuje so na hesła druhich programow, na př. waše "
"hesło póstoweho konta w KMailu."

#: passwords.cpp:70
msgid ""
"You can specify how long kdesu will remember your passwords. A short timeout "
"is more secure than a long timeout."
msgstr ""
"Tu móžeće nastajić, kak dołho sej kdesu waše hesła spomjatkuje. "
"Krótki čas je wěsćiši hač dołhi čas."

#: passwords.cpp:73
msgid "&Timeout:"
msgstr "&Čas spomjatkowanja:"

#: passwords.cpp:76
msgid " min"
msgstr " mjeń."

#: passwords.cpp:189
msgid ""
"<h1>Passwords</h1> This module gives you options for configuring the way in "
"which the \"kdesu\" program treats passwords. Kdesu will ask you for a "
"password when you try to carry out some privileged actions, such as changing "
"the date/time stored in your system clock, or adding new users on your "
"computer."
"<p> You can configure the type of visual feedback given when you type a "
"password, and whether kdesu should remember passwords for some time after "
"you have given them."
"<p> Note that these settings affect <em>only</em>"
" kdesu. This means that the behavior of passwords in KMail and other "
"programs cannot be configured here."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Hesła</h1> Tutón modul wam opcije k dispoziciji staja, zo móžeće "
"nastajić, kak \"kdesu\" z hesłami wobchadźa. Kdesu budźe so za "
"wuwjedźenje priwiligowaneje akcije za hesłom prašeć, na př. za "
"změnjenje systemoweho časa abo dodawanje nowych wužiwarjow."
"<p> Móžeće wizuelnu kontrolu při zapodawanju hesła nastajić a hač ma "
"sej kdesu hesła wěsty čas po zapodaću spomjatkować."
"<p> Wopomńće, zo so tute nastajenja <em>jenož</em>"
" na kdesu poćahuja. To rěka, zo so wobchadźenje z hesłami w KMailu abo "
"druhich programach tu njehodźi nastajić."

